PATCH 518: eleven map-screen glyph plates emitted as a bare arg-less `lcall [0x6b4]`.

A correct scan of build/fist.c -- functions whose ENTIRE body is
`(*(code *)fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c6b4)))(); return;` -- finds 48 such handlers.  Eleven of
them are the map-screen glyph plates, in three shapes:

  simple  `mov ax,K ; add ax,[0x7b9c] ; lea bx,[bx+4] ; lcall [0x6b4]`
      50a2 K=0x0fd8   51be 0x1000   520f 0x1010   5299 0x1020   52e3 0x1030   534f 0x1040

  mode-selected  `mov ax,K ; cmpw [0x7b9e],M ; jne .. ; add ax,[0x7b9c] ; lea bx,[bx+4] ; lcall`
      53af K=0x1050 M=0x18

  edit-gated  `testb [0x6dab],2 ; je .. ; mov ax,K ; cmpw [0x7b9e],M ; jne .. ; add ax,[0x7b9c] ;
               jmp .. ; <else> mov ax,K2 ; lea bx,[bx+4] ; lcall`
      50ea K=0x0fe8 M=0x19 K2=0x0ff8    5486 0x1080/0x1b/0x1090
      5555 0x1098 M=0x1a K2=0x10a8      56af 0x10b0/0x1c/0x10c0

word[DGROUP:0x7b9c] is the map palette/glyph base, word[0x7b9e] the active map mode and byte[0x6dab] bit1
the EDIT-mode flag (the same flag patch 246's neighbourhood calls "enter EDITING mode").  BX is the
display-list element's DGROUP NEAR OFFSET, which BOTH the 2057 and 209e walks publish to DGROUP:0x3e08
(`mov [0x3e08],bx`) immediately before dispatching; the port's dispatch cannot carry it, so it is read
back from there, exactly as patches 503/504/509 do.

Ghidra emitted the entire body of each as a bare arg-less `lcall [0x6b4]`, so the paint service ran with
whatever AX and BX happened to hold -- no glyph id and no element.  These are the map/editor screens, a
surface the goal names explicitly.
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -15021,7 +15021,15 @@
 void __allregs FUN_0000_50a2(void)
 
 {
-  (*(code *)fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c6b4)))();
+  /* PATCH 518: `mov ax,0xfd8 ; add ax,[0x7b9c] ; lea bx,[bx+4] ; lcall [0x6b4]` (asm 0x50a2-0x50b0), a map-screen glyph plate the 2057/209e
+   * display-list walks dispatch.  BX is the list element's DGROUP NEAR OFFSET, which both walks publish
+   * to DGROUP:0x3e08 before dispatching; the port's dispatch cannot carry it, so it is read back there.
+   * Ghidra emitted the ENTIRE body as a bare arg-less `lcall [0x6b4]` -- no glyph id, no BX. */
+  unsigned char *dg = (unsigned char *)g_mem + 0x1c000;
+  unsigned short bx = (unsigned short)(*(unsigned short *)(dg + 0x3e08) + 4);   /* lea bx,[bx+4] */
+  unsigned short ax;
+  ax = (unsigned short)(0xfd8 + *(unsigned short *)(dg + 0x7b9c));
+  (*(code *)fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c6b4)))(ax,bx);
   return;
 }
 
